          "description": "\"was the first researcher studying the mountain's seismic tremors continuously\" admits a fully grammatical reduced-relative-clause reading (\"...the first researcher [who was] studying X\"), analogous to standard constructions like \"she was the first woman running for that office.\" This is a genuinely competing parse to the intended \"the first researcher to study X\" (ordinal + infinitive-of-achievement) reading. The appositive \"an effort that greatly improved eruption forecasting methods\" and the ordinal \"first\" do bias a careful reader toward the intended infinitive reading, and this is a documented, legitimate ETS-style construction (ordinal/superlative + infinitive), so this falls short of an outright critical failure — but the alternate parse is real enough that the item should not pass without strengthening the context.",
